68
00:03:42,984 --> 00:03:44,384
So, you know, let's just jump into it.

69
00:03:44,484 --> 00:03:45,984
Consider a market that's selling off.

70
00:03:45,984 --> 00:03:51,084
In order for the trend to reverse from going down to going up, conditions have to change.

71
00:03:51,784 --> 00:03:54,784
So in a downtrending market, sellers are in control generally.

72
00:03:54,884 --> 00:04:00,684
You know, I say generally. Obviously, if the market's going down, sellers are pushing it down.

73
00:04:01,084 --> 00:04:03,584
There's going to be times when that's not necessarily the case.

74
00:04:03,584 --> 00:04:10,284
There's just going to be no support in the market, not enough bidders, and the market is just drifting lower.

75
00:04:10,384 --> 00:04:14,184
I hate to use the term drifting lower, but there's not enough support.

76
00:04:14,184 --> 00:04:21,684
There are always buyers and sellers in the market. And sometimes there's just not enough buyers to support the market.

77
00:04:22,084 --> 00:04:24,449
So for a market to turn, buyers have

78
00:04:24,449 --> 00:04:28,883
to take control by coming into the market with sufficient quantities to overwhelm the sellers.

79
00:04:31,584 --> 00:04:32,784
For example, here's a 10-year chart.

80
00:04:32,984 --> 00:04:34,284
We're going down, making new lows.

81
00:04:34,584 --> 00:04:36,484
This red line here is the lows.

82
00:04:38,484 --> 00:04:41,984
You hit the bottom, you know, right here, you have a divergence, you have a ratio.

83
00:04:42,184 --> 00:04:45,384
You know, I talk about the ratios, the small prints, the single prints.

84
00:04:46,184 --> 00:04:51,384
And you're seeing a shift in the market, in the control of the market.

85
00:04:51,384 --> 00:04:53,784
You know, earlier sellers were in control.

86
00:04:54,384 --> 00:04:56,284
Now all of a sudden you see buyers take control.

87
00:04:59,188 --> 00:05:00,116
So alternatively, in

88
00:05:00,116 --> 00:05:01,354
a selling off, in

89
00:05:01,354 --> 00:05:05,687
a market selling off, the market can turn when the last seller has sold.

90
00:05:06,288 --> 00:05:12,288
It's not always a case, a clear-cut case where buyers are taking control.

91
00:05:12,588 --> 00:05:20,088
When there's no more sellers to move the market lower, the market will just naturally rise.

92
00:05:21,388 --> 00:05:26,488
Imagine there's sellers coming in, selling, selling.

93
00:05:26,688 --> 00:05:31,088
At some point, the sellers just have no more interest to sell.

94
00:05:31,188 --> 00:05:34,388
When the last seller has sold, that's going to be your bottom.

95
00:05:35,388 --> 00:05:38,688
So, you know, when there's no more selling interest by traders, who's left to sell? Nobody.

96
00:05:39,088 --> 00:05:42,988
Prices have, you know, basically no other way to go except to up.

97
00:05:43,488 --> 00:05:45,024
However, if there's not strong buying

98
00:05:45,024 --> 00:05:46,560
coming in, you know, buyers don't

99
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:49,888
take control, the market can trade sideways until either side takes control again.

100
00:05:51,188 --> 00:05:53,888
I mean, there's always going to be buyers, there's always going to be sellers.

101
00:05:54,188 --> 00:05:58,488
One side is going to be the dominant over the other.

102
00:05:59,788 --> 00:06:03,288
But, you know, if a market is trending lower, there's going to be active selling.

103
00:06:03,788 --> 00:06:07,388
But, you know, once all the sellers have pretty much exhausted themselves,

104
00:06:08,888 --> 00:06:10,188
the buyers are there still.

105
00:06:11,388 --> 00:06:13,205
If people need to buy, but

106
00:06:13,205 --> 00:06:15,022
there's nobody selling at these low

107
00:06:15,022 --> 00:06:16,839
prices, it's just going to start

108
00:06:16,839 --> 00:06:21,686
