109
00:06:22,088 --> 00:06:24,188
So consider a market that's rallying.

110
00:06:24,888 --> 00:06:28,688
In order for the trend to reverse from going up, up to going down, conditions have to change.

111
00:06:29,488 --> 00:06:32,588
In an uptrending market, buyers are in control generally.

112
00:06:32,688 --> 00:06:33,888
Again, I say generally.

113
00:06:35,088 --> 00:06:37,515
There's times where you're in an

114
00:06:37,515 --> 00:06:39,942
uptrend and the market is very

115
00:06:39,942 --> 00:06:43,987
weak at that high uptrend and buyers are starting to...

116
00:06:44,488 --> 00:06:46,788
Weakened and sellers are starting to take control.

117
00:06:46,788 --> 00:06:49,088
The market may not just necessarily be going down.

118
00:06:49,088 --> 00:06:49,858
You know, you

119
00:06:49,858 --> 00:06:51,654
could be making a, forming a weak

120
00:06:51,654 --> 00:06:53,450
high in the sense that, you know,

121
00:06:53,450 --> 00:06:56,786
there's just buying is getting less and less until there's no more buyers.

122
00:06:57,088 --> 00:07:01,209
So for a market to turn, sellers have to take control by

123
00:07:01,209 --> 00:07:04,987
coming into the market with sufficient supply to overwhelm the buyers.

124
00:07:07,356 --> 00:07:08,398
So, again, alternatively, when

125
00:07:08,398 --> 00:07:10,483
